notes.body:
That would work for me. "Contrib" sound like a good enough name. It will involve some work, to ensure, that everything is behaving identical to "Global", but that work should only extend to the ui, so the abstraction by ProfileModel will help there. The main difference should be, that now - with global - an automatic copy get's generated, everytime the profile is selected. With "contrib" it should behave more on the lines of the default profile, in where a copy only gets created if the profile will require a change. That is indeed tricky, but I think doable. Copying a profile by default will only clutter the hard disks with a lot of duplicates, and that might be more confusing.

I am happy to do the extra work, and all duplication checks are already there yet. I'll work on the next iteration and keep you updated.

@BettyD that works for you too with having an extra contrib section? It basically means, that everyone who wants to change your profile, needs to copy first, but that should not be that big of an issue.

